    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0421" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 701.6211/452</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Alien Property Custodian</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Palmer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received June 1.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It has been reported to me as Alien
                    Property Custodian that the German Government owns in the District of Columbia,
                    51,000 square feet of land of the approximate value of $150,000 situated <pb
                        facs="0422" n="338" xml:id="pg338"/> on the north side of S Street, between
                    Phelps Place and 23d Street, Northwest.</p>
                <p>It will be noticed that this property is distinct from the site of the German
                    Legation [<hi rendition="#italic">Embassy</hi>] and disconnected therewith.</p>
                <p>I shall appreciate your consideration of this matter, in connection with the
                    former rulings of your Department, and your advice as to whether this property
                    is subject to a proper demand of my office.</p>
                <p>Yours respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Mitchell Palmer</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
